<!-- ── CHAPTER 01: Meet The Artist ── -->
<section class="mm-story-section" id="mm-story">
  <div class="mm-article">
    <div class="mm-chapter mm-reveal">
      <div class="mm-chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mm-chapter-label">Meet The Artist</div>
        <h2 class="mm-chapter-title">Talent Was Never<br><em>The Problem.</em></h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mm-body-copy mm-reveal">
      Max Motion is an independent artist who, like most musicians at his level, had the harder thing already figured out. <strong>The music was good.</strong> Listeners who found it stayed with it. The drops hit. The mixes were clean. The vision was clear.
    </p>

    <p class="mm-body-copy mm-reveal">
      What he didn't have was <em>reach</em>. Sitting at <strong>4,000 monthly listeners</strong>, Max was caught in the same trap hundreds of thousands of other independent artists know by heart. Talent doesn't pay rent. Streams, shows, events, and brand deals do. And without that first step of garnering streams, going all-in on music meant betting against a financial reality that wasn't going to budge on its own.
    </p>

    <p class="mm-body-copy mm-reveal">
      He had momentum, an audience, and a ceiling that had stopped moving. Streaming is one of the most saturated, algorithm-driven corners of the music industry, and breaking through doesn't happen by uploading harder. <strong>It happens by being placed in front of the people who actually want what you make.</strong>
    </p>

    <blockquote class="mm-pull-quote mm-reveal" style="transition-delay:0.1s;">
      <p>"I knew the music was there. What I needed was for the right people to actually hear it. That's the part nobody tells you, talent alone doesn't move the needle."</p>
      <cite>— Max Motion</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── CHAPTER 02: The Strategy ── -->
<section class="mm-story-section mm-alt">
  <div class="mm-article">
    <div class="mm-chapter mm-reveal">
      <div class="mm-chapter-num" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mm-chapter-label">The Strategy</div>
        <h2 class="mm-chapter-title">A System Built For<br><em>Max's Music.</em></h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mm-body-copy mm-reveal">
      GPM's approach with Max wasn't generic playlist pitching. <strong>Every genre has its own audience anatomy</strong>, different listening habits, different playlist ecosystems, different algorithmic triggers, and the campaign was built around Max's sound specifically. Three phases, executed in sequence, each one feeding the next.
    </p>

    <ol class="mm-timeline mm-reveal" style="transition-delay:0.05s;">
      <li class="mm-timeline-item">
        <div class="mm-timeline-phase">Phase 01 · Audience Expansion</div>
        <div class="mm-timeline-title">Genre-Specific Targeting</div>
        <p class="mm-timeline-body">
          Genre-native playlist placements positioned Max's tracks where his ideal listeners already live. No cross-genre noise. No off-target plays. Just real fans of the sound being introduced to an artist they hadn't heard yet.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="mm-timeline-item">
        <div class="mm-timeline-phase">Phase 02 · Momentum Building</div>
        <div class="mm-timeline-title">Multi-Track Catalogue Promotion</div>
        <p class="mm-timeline-body">
          One track gets you a spike. A catalogue gets you compounding. GPM promoted across multiple releases simultaneously so the algorithm started recommending Max as an artist, not just a single song. Performance data fed back into the next round of placements.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="mm-timeline-item">
        <div class="mm-timeline-phase">Phase 03 · Career Transition</div>
        <div class="mm-timeline-title">Sustainable Growth Patterns</div>
        <p class="mm-timeline-body">
          The endgame wasn't a viral moment. It was a foundation. Daily discovery, monthly listener retention, and a streaming presence consistent enough to unlock opportunities that simply weren't on the table at 4K listeners.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="mm-body-copy mm-reveal">
      Within weeks of the campaign launching, Max's catalogue started picking up serious traction. <strong>That early momentum wasn't the ceiling.</strong> It was the starting line for what came next.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

